@mattpocockuk You can either go fast or go straight. It’s really hard to do both.

Many developers I know are choosing to go fast (more code) at the expense of everything else.

So, while I agree that we can still produce software using the same principles we have honed for decades, more and more people are disregarding them because doing more feels better, or is what’s required of them.

@roboguy20 @florian_tramer If you system includes symbolic operations and neural networks, it is by definition neurosymbolic.

Part of the point is that you have access to both you might (at least in principle) then choose what is suitable for a given task.

(Also, i believe that humans are neurosymbolic for many many reasons and not just because a few of them use Lean. If you are genuinely curious, start with my 2001 book The Algebraic Mind)

@trollaxethrower @ChristianL26264 Fast forward a few years and think about what will happen when Anthropic starts claiming ownership on your code, your writing, and everything that they touched. 

Isn’t AI a tool?

Imagine Microsoft watermarking your documents.

@wholemars For me it isn't just beautiful. It's where the autonomous industry tests their robots. 

I took the first video of a Waymo on 280 that was posted to YouTube, for instance.

Oh, and underneath the freeway by Sand Hill Road is a mile-long building. That's where they discovered quarks.

